Note: several aliases intentionally share one address (bit-packed control
words, e.g. MIX_EN/MIX_AUTO_CAL/MIX_SELECT, PIx_PAUSE_P/I/D, and module-level
names like PI_SEL/OUT_SEL). This is not a bug. get_register_info reports them as
`aliases_sharing_address`; set_parameter refuses whole-register writes to them.
Use the per-field alias (e.g. MIX_SELECT[2]) via set_signal_path.
